{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Not His children.</b> Those who say they are not His children, and likewise \"children\" — no faithfulness is in them. The reason: they do not acknowledge that He created them, and if they acknowledge with the mouth, they do not acknowledge with the heart; the proof is that they do not fear HaShem. And according to the one who says לו [to Him], he served himself, and afterward with him [n: reading uncertain; the phrase is elliptical and possibly corrupt], and it is their blemish, and the meaning: because of their blemish, that it is a twisted and crooked generation." "<b>And crooked.</b> One who persists and contends in his stubbornness, and likewise נפתולי אלהים [Genesis 30:8]. Some say that the meaning of שחת לו is like שחתו להם, and the meaning refers to the soul [n: לנפש׳ appears abbreviated; expanded as לנפשה or similar, exact form uncertain]. And do not wonder because the word is singular, for so is the rule of the letter he; do you not see זכור ימות עולם [remember the days of eternity], between years of generation and generation? And what is correct in my eyes is thus: שחת לו [they dealt corruptly to Him], and the meaning is corrupting the ways of HaShem, the planted ones and the statutes that He commanded, as if it said: they dealt corruptly to Him, a crooked generation that is not His children, and this is their blemish. And the proof is that so is the interpretation of what comes after it, namely הלהם תגמלו זאת [Is this how you requite YHWH?]. And I have already explained the meaning of the letter he in the book Moznayim."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:52.251099485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}